---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="How Memflex works — System 1 + System 2" desc="Every request is checked against memory in <10ms. Hits answer instantly at ₹0; misses think once, then become memory." path="/how-it-works">
<div class="wrap" style="padding:64px 24px 20px">
  <span class="eyebrow">How it works</span>
  <h1>Check memory.<br />Think on novelty.<br />Never trust blindly.</h1>
  <p class="lead">Three mechanisms, each tested. This page mirrors the implementation in <code>reflex/</code> — not a metaphor.</p>
</div>

<section class="block">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>1 · The reflex check (&lt;10ms)</h2>
    <p class="lead">Embed → vector search → calibrated score → gate.</p>
    <div class="card" style="margin-top:22px;overflow-x:auto">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 960 300" width="100%" style="min-width:640px;display:block" role="img" aria-label="Request flow diagram">
        <defs>
          <marker id="ar" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="7" refY="4" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L8,4 L0,8" fill="none" stroke="#c8ff2e" stroke-width="1.6"/></marker>
        </defs>
        <rect x="8" y="120" width="150" height="60" rx="10" fill="#141417" stroke="#232329"/>
        <text x="83" y="145" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ededf0" font-size="14" font-weight="700">Agent request</text>
        <text x="83" y="163" text-anchor="middle" fill="#9d9da8" font-size="12">any language</text>
        <rect x="210" y="110" width="170" height="80" rx="10" fill="#141417" stroke="#c8ff2e"/>
        <text x="295" y="138" text-anchor="middle" fill="#c8ff2e" font-size="14" font-weight="700">REFLEX CHECK</text>
        <text x="295" y="157" text-anchor="middle" fill="#9d9da8" font-size="12">embed + search + score</text>
        <text x="295" y="173" text-anchor="middle" fill="#6b6b76" font-size="12">&lt;10ms</text>
        <line x1="158" y1="150" x2="205" y2="150" stroke="#c8ff2e" stroke-width="1.6" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <rect x="440" y="40" width="200" height="80" rx="10" fill="#141417" stroke="#232329"/>
        <text x="540" y="68" text-anchor="middle" fill="#c8ff2e" font-size="14" font-weight="700">SERVE FROM MEMORY</text>
        <text x="540" y="87" text-anchor="middle" fill="#9d9da8" font-size="12">~0–50ms · ₹0 · 0 LLM calls</text>
        <text x="540" y="103" text-anchor="middle" fill="#6b6b76" font-size="12">score ≥ 0.85</text>
        <rect x="440" y="180" width="200" height="80" rx="10" fill="#141417" stroke="#232329"/>
        <text x="540" y="208" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffb86b" font-size="14" font-weight="700">LLM (System 2)</text>
        <text x="540" y="227" text-anchor="middle" fill="#9d9da8" font-size="12">OpenAI · Claude · Gemini · Ollama…</text>
        <text x="540" y="243" text-anchor="middle" fill="#6b6b76" font-size="12">novelty only</text>
        <line x1="380" y1="130" x2="435" y2="80" stroke="#c8ff2e" stroke-width="1.6" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <line x1="380" y1="170" x2="435" y2="220" stroke="#ffb86b" stroke-width="1.6" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <rect x="700" y="180" width="220" height="80" rx="10" fill="#141417" stroke="#232329"/>
        <text x="810" y="208" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ededf0" font-size="14" font-weight="700">DISTILL → SAVE</text>
        <text x="810" y="227" text-anchor="middle" fill="#9d9da8" font-size="12">confidence 0.8 · TTL inferred</text>
        <text x="810" y="243" text-anchor="middle" fill="#6b6b76" font-size="12">next time: System 1</text>
        <line x1="640" y1="220" x2="695" y2="220" stroke="#6b6b76" stroke-width="1.6" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
      </svg>
    </div>
    <div class="tabs" style="margin-top:18px">
      <div class="tab-btns"><button class="on">Score formula</button><button>Explain mode</button></div>
      <div class="tab-pane on"><div class="codeblock"><button class="copy">Copy</button><pre>score = 0.6·similarity        # how close is this situation?
      + 0.2·hit_consistency   # has this reflex been right before?
      + 0.1·recency           # when was it last verified?
      − 0.5·correction_rate   # how often was it overruled?

score ≥ 0.85 → reflex      # pure memory, zero LLM calls
0.65 – 0.85  → reverify     # memory + background re-check
score &lt; 0.65 → llm       # novel: think, distill, save</pre></div></div>
      <div class="tab-pane"><div class="codeblock"><button class="copy">Copy</button><pre>POST /ask  &#123;"message": "refund??", "explain": true&#125;

&#123;
  "answer": "Your refund is being processed…",
  "source": "reflex",
  "similarity": 0.98,          # why this memory matched
  "matched_situation": "hii what status refund",
  "expanded_from": "Hii what is status for my refund",  # follow-up trail
  "threshold": 0.85
&#125;</pre></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>2 · Memory that corrects itself</h2>
    <div class="grid3" style="margin-top:22px">
      <div class="card rv"><h3>👎 buries mistakes</h3><p>A thumbs-down drops confidence 0.08 and counts a correction. ~3 reports push any reflex below the band — the next ask goes back to the LLM, which re-learns into the same record.</p></div>
      <div class="card rv"><h3>TTL is a hard wall</h3><p><em>Processing / ETA / status</em> answers auto-expire in 1 day; stable FAQs live 30. Expired memory is never served — it re-thinks instead.</p></div>
      <div class="card rv"><h3>Verification loop</h3><p>Every 24h, stale reflexes are re-asked to the LLM: CONFIRM bumps the timestamp, CONFLICT slashes confidence. Run it manually: <code>POST /verify/run</code>.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>3 · Follow-ups resolve like a human would</h2>
    <p class="lead">Day 1: <em>“Hii what is status for my refund”</em> → Day 2: <em>“refund??”</em> → same answer. Single-token queries expand from your last message (persistent, restart-proof); no history, no expansion — safe miss instead.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block" id="try">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow rv">Try it yourself</span>
    <h2 class="rv">4 · Ask twice. Watch the flip.</h2>
    <p class="lead rv">First ask thinks (<b>LLM badge</b>). Same ask again — memory answers, ₹0 (<b>REFLEX badge</b>). Needs a running server.</p>
    <div class="card rv" style="margin-top:24px">
      <div class="askrow" style="margin-top:0">
        <select id="trymodel" aria-label="Model">
          <option value="gemini/gemini-flash-latest" selected>gemini — Google Gemini</option>
          <option value="openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-chat">openrouter — DeepSeek via OpenRouter</option>
          <option value="mock/mock-echo">mock — instant, keyless</option>
        </select>
        <input id="tryq" type="text" maxlength="300" value="When will my refund arrive?" aria-label="Your question" />
        <input id="tryttl" type="number" min="1" max="365" placeholder="TTL days (auto)" aria-label="Memory TTL in days" style="max-width:150px" title="How many days this answer stays in memory. Blank = auto (1 day for changing facts, 30 for stable ones)." />
        <button class="btn btn-primary" id="trybtn">Ask</button>
      </div>
      <div class="muted" style="margin-top:14px;font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:.08em">CUSTOMER SUPPORT BOTS</div>
      <div class="chips" style="margin-top:8px">
        <span class="trychip">When will my refund arrive?</span>
        <span class="trychip">¿Dónde está mi entrega?</span>
        <span class="trychip">Cancel my order, please</span>
      </div>
      <div class="muted" style="margin-top:12px;font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:.08em">TICKET TRIAGE &amp; ROUTING</div>
      <div class="chips" style="margin-top:8px">
        <span class="trychip">Route this: charged twice, need billing help</span>
        <span class="trychip">Wo ist meine Rückerstattung?</span>
        <span class="trychip">Delivery is late, where is my package?</span>
      </div>
      <div class="muted" style="margin-top:12px;font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:.08em">VOICE AGENTS &amp; LIVE CHAT</div>
      <div class="chips" style="margin-top:8px">
        <span class="trychip">Refund status?</span>
        <span class="trychip">Cancel order</span>
        <span class="trychip">My delivery?</span>
      </div>
      <div id="tryans" class="tryans" aria-live="polite"><span class="muted">Your answer lands here — with the badge that proves where it came from.</span></div>
      <div class="muted" style="margin-top:10px;font-size:13px"><span id="trystatus">● checking connection…</span> · <span id="trycount">this page: 0 LLM calls · 0 reflex answers</span></div>
      <p class="muted" style="font-size:13px;margin-top:10px">This demo talks to a Memflex API — by default one on your own machine (<code>python3 -m reflex.api.app</code>). Mock needs nothing; Gemini needs a server-side key.</p>
      <details style="margin-top:8px"><summary class="muted" style="cursor:pointer;font-size:13px">Using a hosted API instead?</summary>
        <div class="askrow" style="margin-top:10px">
          <input id="tryapi" type="text" value="http://localhost:8000" aria-label="API base URL" />
        </div>
        <p class="muted" style="font-size:13px">Paste a public Memflex API URL and the playground talks to that server instead. Saved in this browser only.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top:26px"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/docs#quickstart">Try it in 5 minutes</a></div>
  </div>
</section>
<script>
(function () {
  let nLlm = 0, nRef = 0;
  const $ = id => document.getElementById(id);
  const DEFAULT_API = 'http://localhost:8000';
  function apiBase() {
    try { return (localStorage.getItem('mx_api') || DEFAULT_API).replace(/\/$/, ''); }
    catch (e) { return DEFAULT_API; }
  }
  try {
    const saved = localStorage.getItem('mx_api');
    if (saved && $('tryapi')) $('tryapi').value = saved;
  } catch (e) {}
  if ($('tryapi')) $('tryapi').addEventListener('change', () => {
    try { localStorage.setItem('mx_api', $('tryapi').value.trim()); } catch (e) {}
    ping(apiBase());
  });
  const esc = s => String(s == null ? '' : s).replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;');
  document.querySelectorAll('.trychip').forEach(c => c.addEventListener('click', () => { $('tryq').value = c.textContent; }));
  async function postOnce(base, payload) {
    const r = await fetch(base + '/ask', {
      method: 'POST', headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
      body: JSON.stringify(payload),
    });
    if (!r.ok) throw new Error('HTTP ' + r.status);
    return r.json();
  }
  async function ping(base) {
    // Connection dot: green = server reachable from YOUR browser, red = not.
    const dot = $('trystatus');
    if (!/^https?:\/\//i.test(base)) {
      dot.innerHTML = '<span style="color:#ffb86b">● bad URL — must start with http(s)://</span>';
      return false;
    }
    dot.innerHTML = '<span style="color:#9d9da8">● checking…</span>';
    try {
      const ctl = new AbortController();
      const t = setTimeout(() => ctl.abort(), 6000);
      const r = await fetch(base + '/health', { signal: ctl.signal });
      clearTimeout(t);
      if (!r.ok) throw new Error('HTTP ' + r.status);
      dot.innerHTML = '<span style="color:#c8ff2e">● connected</span>';
      return true;
    } catch (e) {
      dot.innerHTML = '<span style="color:#ff6b6b">● unreachable — is the server running?</span>';
      return false;
    }
  }
  ping(apiBase());
  $('trybtn').addEventListener('click', async () => {
    const base = apiBase();
    const msg = $('tryq').value.trim();
    const model = $('trymodel').value;
    const ttlRaw = ($('tryttl').value || '').trim();
    const ttl = /^\d+$/.test(ttlRaw) ? Math.min(365, Math.max(1, parseInt(ttlRaw, 10))) : null;
    if (!msg) { $('tryq').focus(); return; }
    const btn = $('trybtn');
    btn.disabled = true; btn.textContent = 'Asking…';
    $('tryans').innerHTML = '<span class="muted">Thinking… (novel) or remembering… (seen before)</span>';
    const t0 = performance.now();
    const payload = { user_id: 'try-playground', message: msg, llm: model };
    if (ttl !== null) payload.ttl_days = ttl;
    let d = null, err = '';
    for (let attempt = 1; attempt <= 2 && !d; attempt++) {
      try { d = await postOnce(base, payload); }
      catch (e) { err = String((e && e.message) || e); await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 800)); }
    }
    if (d) {
      const ms = Math.round(performance.now() - t0);
      const isReflex = d.source !== 'llm';
      if (isReflex) nRef++; else nLlm++;
      $('trycount').textContent = 'this page: ' + nLlm + ' LLM calls · ' + nRef + ' reflex answers';
      const badge = isReflex
        ? '<span class="trybadge go">REFLEX — memory, ₹0</span>'
        : '<span class="trybadge wait">LLM — thought + memorized</span>';
      $('tryans').innerHTML = badge +
        '<div style="margin-top:10px">' + esc(d.answer) + '</div>' +
        '<div class="muted" style="margin-top:8px;font-size:13px">confidence ' + d.confidence +
        ' · server ' + d.latency_ms + 'ms · browser ' + ms + 'ms</div>' +
        (isReflex ? '' : '<div class="muted" style="font-size:13px">Ask the exact same again — watch it flip to REFLEX.</div>');
    } else {
      // Diagnose precisely: is the server down, or did /ask itself fail
      // (e.g. Gemini model without a server-side key → HTTP 502)?
      let diagnosis = 'server is down or unreachable from your browser — on the public site this usually means no API is running on your machine (start one locally) or you need a hosted API URL (see above)';
      try {
        const h = await fetch(base + '/health');
        if (h.ok) diagnosis = '/ask failed (' + esc(err) + ') — server is up, so check the model: Gemini needs a server-side key, try mock instead';
      } catch (e) { /* health also failed — server down */ }
      $('tryans').innerHTML = '<span class="muted">No answer: ' + diagnosis +
        '. Verify: <code>curl ' + esc(base) + '/health</code></span>';
    }
    btn.disabled = false; btn.textContent = 'Ask';
  });
})();
</script>
</Base>
